{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וטהרתם", :translit "u-tiharatem", :gloss "and you shall purify"} {:he "ואידך וזרקתי עליכם מים טהורים וטהרתם", :translit "ve-idach ve-zaraketi aleichem mayim tehorim u-tiharatem", :gloss "and the other: and I will sprinkle upon you pure water and you shall be purified"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וטהרתם"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase \"וטהרתם\" appears in Ezekiel 36:25 in the context of purification through sprinkling: \"וזרקתי עליכם מים טהורים וטהרתם.\" The laws of hag'alah — purifying vessels by boiling — are detailed in rabbinic law; see tractate Avodah Zarah 75a–76a for the principles of kashering vessels taken from non-Jews. The Ba'al HaTurim links the two occurrences of \"וטהרתם\" to show that in Numbers 31:23–24 Moses was taught not only hag'alah but also purification via sprinkling (הזאה).", :sources ["Ezekiel 36:25" "Avodah Zarah 75a–76a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וטהרתם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וטהרתם", :refs ["Numbers 31:24" "Ezekiel 36:25"], :n 2, :lens :exact}]}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:32:17.970343715Z", :model "glm-5.2"}